IMPORT prelude

-- Limitation Act 1981 (NT), child abuse provisions -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library.
-- The provisions encoded here need three things of a date: whether one day is before another (s 53(1) "before the
-- commencement"), the day a person turns 18 (s 5A(6) "under 18 years of age"), and the calendar day itself.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Not an official version of the Limitation Act 1981 (NT). Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is
-- owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted under the Northern Territory copyright policy of 8 October 1996; see
-- SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the child abuse provisions`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `falls before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The 18th birthday: the same day and month 18 years on; a person born on 29 February turns 18 on 28 February of a
-- year that has none (fork F2 in NOTES.md). A person is "under 18 years of age" up to the end of the day before it.
GIVEN `the birth day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the 18th birthday of a person born on` `the birth day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the birth day`) (`the number of days in month` (DATE_MONTH `the birth day`) `of` `the year of turning 18`)) (DATE_MONTH `the birth day`) `the year of turning 18`
    WHERE
        `the year of turning 18` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the birth day` PLUS 18
